{"name":"Miracle at Wrigley","hex":"#255ba2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"miracle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An event that appears inexplicable by the laws of nature and so is held to be supernatural in origin.","A fortunate outcome that prevails despite overwhelming odds against it."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To affect by a miracle; to work a miracle upon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miracle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Miracle","blocks":[{"text":"A miracle is an event that cannot be explained by natural or scientific laws and accordingly gets attributed to some supernatural or preternatural cause. Various religions often attribute a phenomenon characterized as miraculous to the actions of a supernatural being, especially by a deity, a miracle worker, a saint, or a religious leader."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miracle","wikidata":"Q170774"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Tintoretto_-_Miracle_of_the_Slave.jpg/500px-Tintoretto_-_Miracle_of_the_Slave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Tintoretto_-_Miracle_of_the_Slave.jpg/1280px-Tintoretto_-_Miracle_of_the_Slave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Tintoretto_-_Miracle_of_the_Slave.jpg/500px-Tintoretto_-_Miracle_of_the_Slave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Miracle of the Slave, a 1548 painting by Tintoretto, from the Gallerie dell'Accademia in Venice. It portrays an episode of the life of Saint Mark, patron saint of Venice, taken from Jacobus de Voragine's Golden Legend. The scene shows a saint intervening to make a slave who is about to be martyred invulnerable.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATintoretto_-_Miracle_of_